
# Catch the Falling Dot Game — Connection Table

## 1. Components

- Arduino Uno × 1
- SN74HC595N shift register IC × 2
- 1088AS 8×8 LED matrix × 1
- Push buttons × 2
- 1 kΩ resistors × 8 (SEG lines)
- 2.2 kΩ resistors × 8 (DIG lines)
- Breadboard and jumper wires
- USB cable

## 2. Arduino Uno to Shift Registers

| Arduino Pin | Connection | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| D2 | IC1 pin 14 (SER) | Serial data |
| D3 | Both ICs pin 12 (RCLK) | Latch |
| D4 | Both ICs pin 11 (SRCLK) | Shift clock |
| 5V | Both ICs pin 16 (VCC) | Power |
| GND | Both ICs pin 8 (GND) | Ground |
| 5V | Both ICs pin 10 (SRCLR) | Disable clear |
| GND | Both ICs pin 13 (OE) | Enable outputs |
| IC1 pin 9 (QH') | IC2 pin 14 (SER) | Daisy-chain data |

## 3. IC1 to LED Matrix — DIG Rows

Each DIG line uses a 2.2 kΩ series resistor in the current setup.

| Matrix Signal | Matrix Pin | IC1 Output | IC1 Pin | Resistor |
|---|---:|---|---:|---|
| DIG0 | 9 | Q0 | 15 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG1 | 14 | Q1 | 1 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG2 | 8 | Q2 | 2 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG3 | 12 | Q3 | 3 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG4 | 1 | Q4 | 4 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG5 | 7 | Q5 | 5 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG6 | 2 | Q6 | 6 | 2.2 kΩ |
| DIG7 | 5 | Q7 | 7 | 2.2 kΩ |

## 4. IC2 to LED Matrix — SEG Columns

Each SEG line uses an individual 1 kΩ series resistor.

| Matrix Signal | Matrix Pin | IC2 Output | IC2 Pin | Resistor |
|---|---:|---|---:|---|
| SEG A | 3 | Q0 | 15 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG B | 4 | Q1 | 1 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG C | 10 | Q2 | 2 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG D | 6 | Q3 | 3 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG E | 11 | Q4 | 4 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG F | 15 | Q5 | 5 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG G | 16 | Q6 | 6 | 1 kΩ |
| SEG DP | 13 | Q7 | 7 | 1 kΩ |

Note: The SEG output mapping above assumes the outputs are connected in A, B, C, D, E, F, G, DP order. Verify against the actual wiring.

## 5. Push Buttons

| Button | Arduino Pin | Other Terminal | Code Configuration |
|---|---|---|---|
| Left button | D5 | GND | INPUT_PULLUP |
| Right button | D6 | GND | INPUT_PULLUP |

External resistors are not required for the push buttons when using the Arduino's internal pull-ups.

## 6. Shift Register Power Connections

For both SN74HC595N ICs:

- Pin 16 (VCC) -> Arduino 5V
- Pin 8 (GND) -> Arduino GND
- Pin 10 (SRCLR) -> Arduino 5V
- Pin 13 (OE) -> Arduino GND

Recommended: Place a 0.1 µF ceramic decoupling capacitor between VCC and GND near each IC.

## 7. Game Operation

1. A single LED falls from the top of the matrix.
2. The two-LED paddle appears at the bottom.
3. Press the left button to move the paddle left.
4. Press the right button to move the paddle right.
5. Catch the falling LED to increase the score.
6. Successful catches increase the falling speed.
7. Three missed dots end the game.
8. Press either button to restart.

## 8. Electrical Safety Notes

- Disconnect USB power before changing wiring.
- Check the SN74HC595N datasheet for output and total package-current limits.
- The existing 2.2 kΩ DIG resistors may limit row current enough to make the display dim or unreliable.
- Series resistors alone do not guarantee safe operation for every LED pattern.
- Verify the exact 1088AS matrix pinout and polarity before making changes.
